{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring Framework supports registering beans in a functional way by using lambdas as an alternative to XML or Java configuration ("
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Bean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "). In a nutshell, it lets you register beans with a lambda that acts as a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "FactoryBean"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This mechanism is very efficient, as it does not require any reflection or CGLIB proxies."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In Java, you can, for example, write the following:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "class Foo {}\n\nclass Bar {\n\tprivate final Foo foo;\n\tpublic Bar(Foo foo) {\n\t\tthis.foo = foo;\n\t}\n}\n\nGenericApplicationContext context = new GenericApplicationContext();\ncontext.registerBean(Foo.class);\ncontext.registerBean(Bar.class, () -> new Bar(context.getBean(Foo.class)));"
          }
        ],
        "language": "java",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In Kotlin, with reified type parameters and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "GenericApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " Kotlin extensions, you can instead write the following:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "class Foo\n\nclass Bar(private val foo: Foo)\n\nval context = GenericApplicationContext().apply {\n\tregisterBean<Foo>()\n\tregisterBean { Bar(it.getBean()) }\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "kotlin",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When the class "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Bar"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " has a single constructor, you can even just specify the bean class, the constructor parameters will be autowired by type:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "val context = GenericApplicationContext().apply {\n\tregisterBean<Foo>()\n\tregisterBean<Bar>()\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "kotlin",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In order to allow a more declarative approach and cleaner syntax, Spring Framework provides a "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Kotlin bean definition DSL"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/kdoc-api/spring-context/org.springframework.context.support/-bean-definition-dsl/index.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " It declares an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContextInitializer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " through a clean declarative API, which lets you deal with profiles and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Environment"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for customizing how beans are registered."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the following example notice that:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "ulist",
        "id": null,
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Type inference usually allows to avoid specifying the type for bean references like "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ref(\"bazBean\")"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "It is possible to use Kotlin top level functions to declare beans using callable references like "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bean(::myRouter)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in this example"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When specifying "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bean<Bar>()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bean(::myRouter)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", parameters are autowired by type"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [],
            "checkbox": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "FooBar"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean will be registered only if the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "foobar"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " profile is active"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "style": null,
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "class Foo\nclass Bar(private val foo: Foo)\nclass Baz(var message: String = \"\")\nclass FooBar(private val baz: Baz)\n\nval myBeans = beans {\n\tbean<Foo>()\n\tbean<Bar>()\n\tbean(\"bazBean\") {\n\t\tBaz().apply {\n\t\t\tmessage = \"Hello world\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tprofile(\"foobar\") {\n\t\tbean { FooBar(ref(\"bazBean\")) }\n\t}\n\tbean(::myRouter)\n}\n\nfun myRouter(foo: Foo, bar: Bar, baz: Baz) = router {\n\t// ...\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "kotlin",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "This DSL is programmatic, meaning it allows custom registration logic of beans through an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "if"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " expression, a "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "for"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " loop, or any other Kotlin constructs."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can then use this "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "beans()"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " function to register beans on the application context, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "listing",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "val context = GenericApplicationContext().apply {\n\tmyBeans.initialize(this)\n\trefresh()\n}"
          }
        ],
        "language": "kotlin",
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Spring Boot is based on JavaConfig and "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "does not yet provide specific support for functional bean definition"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/issues/8115"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", but you can experimentally use functional bean definitions through Spring Boot’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContextInitializer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " support. See "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "this Stack Overflow answer"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/45935931/how-to-use-functional-bean-definition-kotlin-dsl-with-spring-boot-and-spring-w/46033685#46033685"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for more details and up-to-date information. See also the experimental Kofu DSL developed in "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Spring Fu incubator"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "link",
            "target": "https://github.com/spring-projects-experimental/spring-fu"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Bean Definition DSL"
      }
    ]
  }
}
